# .md-pressignore — files md-press leaves alone (gitignore syntax).
#
# md-press honors this even when a file is named explicitly, so the commit
# hook (bin/check-commit) does not ask for these to be reformatted, and a
# whole-tree `md-press --fix` cannot touch them. Each group says why. A file
# belongs here only if reformatting it would be wrong even though it renders
# the same: a point-in-time record, a verbatim copy, or a generated file whose
# source is where the fix goes. Live documents do not belong here; fix them.

# Frozen archaeology: superseded material and the records of finished cycles.
# The orientation (CLAUDE.md, "deliberately-frozen archaeology") names these.
.archive/
.integrated/
.archived/
.routing-trail/
.gem-hunt-trail/
LOG.md
msc/reflections/
msc/reflections-rowan-2025-12/
releases/

# Audit records: de-novo first-encounter reports and the per-cycle findings
# written from them. They are what a reader said at the time, kept as said.
audits/AUDIT-WORKING-*/
audits/ADJUDICATION-WORKING-*/
audits/aat-reboot-aux-supplemental/
audits/audit-*-FINAL-*.md
audits/audit-findings-*.md
audits/pending-findings-*.md

# Superseded segments (FORMAT: old-* segments are archaeology, exempt from
# the segment gates).
old-*.md

# Pre-AAT and third-party-derived material.
ref/agentic-tft/
02-tst-core/lit-review/

# Verbatim model outputs: survey answers, prompts as sent, quiz responses.
empirica/glyph-sequence-perception/data/
msc/quiz-responses/

